---
title: The Logs page
description: Follow your bots live, filter the lines by text, level, tag and account, and download what you see as a text file.
appRoute: /logs
---

Want to know what your bots did while you were away? The {% ui key="client:nav.logs" /%} page shows every move, from every account, as it happens.

{% terms_on_page /%}

## Open the logs {% #open %}

Choose {% ui key="client:nav.logs" /%} in the sidebar. Each line is one thing a bot did or saw. The oldest line is at the top and the newest at the bottom. GGE Command keeps the newest 500 {% term id="log" %}log{% /term %} lines of each {% term id="game-account" %}game account{% /term %}, and none older than 7 days.

{% screenshot id="logs" alt="The Logs page: the filters for text, accounts, tags and level at the top, then a list of lines, each with a time, a level, a tag in brackets, an account name and a message." /%}

## Read a line {% #read-a-line %}

Each line has five parts, from left to right:

1. **Time**: your local time. Hover over it to see the full date.
2. **Level**: how serious the line is. See [levels](#levels).
3. **Tag**: the part of the bot that wrote the line, in brackets. Most tags name a {% term id="plugin" %}plugin{% /term %}, such as `[taxCollector]`. Lines about signing in and the connection carry `[ggeBot]`. Each tag keeps its own colour.
4. **Account**: the game account the line belongs to. Hover over it to see the {% term id="server" %}server{% /term %}.
5. **Message**: what happened, in your language.

A divider marks each new day: **Today**, **Yesterday** or the date. Select a tag or an account name in a line to show only the lines with that tag or account.

## The four levels {% #levels %}

- {% ui key="ui:level.info" /%}: normal work, such as an attack sent or taxes collected.
- {% ui key="ui:level.warn" /%}: the game refused something, or something may be off. The bot carries on.
- {% ui key="ui:level.error" /%}: a serious failure or refusal. These lines count in the **Errors** tile on the [Overview page](/war-room/dashboard/#figures).
- {% ui key="ui:level.notNow" /%}: the game refused for now, and it passes by itself. Think of a cooldown, a full queue or too few resources. These lines are not errors, and you usually have nothing to do.

{% aside type="tip" id="errors-first" %}
Something looks wrong? Pick {% ui key="ui:level.error" /%} first, then pick the account. The error codes in the messages are explained on the [error codes page](/errors/).
{% /aside %}

## Follow the lines live {% #follow-live %}

While **Following live** shows above the lines, each new line appears at the bottom and the view stays on it.

Scroll up to read older lines, and following stops. New lines still arrive, and a button counts them: **5 new lines · Jump to latest**. Choose it to go back to the newest line and follow again. Scrolling back to the bottom also follows again.

To hold the view still, choose {% ui key="ui:log.pause" /%}. Choose {% ui key="ui:log.resume" /%} or {% ui key="ui:log.jump" /%} to follow again.

## Filter the lines {% #filters %}

Use the filters above the lines. Every filter you set must match.

- **Filter text**: shows lines whose message or tag contains what you type. Capitals don't matter. Press **/** to jump to this box. The matching text is marked in each line.
- **Accounts**: pick one or more accounts. Each shows how many lines it has.
- **Tags**: pick one or more plugins.
- **Level**: pick **All** or one level, including {% ui key="ui:level.notNow" /%}. Each level shows its count.

The count below the filters says how many lines you see, such as **280 of 280 lines**. Choose {% ui key="ui:log.clearFilters" /%} to show everything again. When older lines are kept, a button at the top loads them.

On a phone, choose **Filters** to open the filter panel. Then choose **Show** to see the lines.

## Your filters stay in the address {% #filters-in-url %}

The page writes your filters into its web address. If you reload the page, your filters are still set. Bookmark a filtered view to open it again later, and use your browser's Back button to undo the last filter you set.

## Download the lines {% #download %}

Choose {% ui key="client:logs.download" /%} to save the lines you see now as a text file. Your filters apply, so filter first if you want only some lines. The file lists one line per row, oldest first:

```
2026-06-15 11:44:42 ERROR [ggeBot] Brightwater: The connection closed: timedOut
```

In the file, the levels are written `INFO`, `WARN`, `ERROR` and `LATER`. `LATER` is a line the game said "{% term id="not-now" %}not now{% /term %}" to.

Choose {% ui key="client:logs.refresh" /%} to load the lines again.

## One account's logs {% #account-logs %}

Open an account from the [Overview page](/war-room/dashboard/#account-drawer) and choose its {% ui key="client:nav.logs" /%} tab. It shows the same live lines for that one account, with the text, level and tag filters.

Two more ways lead to the right lines. On the account's {% ui key="client:drawer.overview" /%} tab, {% ui key="client:overview.errors.seeLogs" /%} opens this page for that account. Under the bell, {% ui key="client:notifications.viewLogs" /%} opens the lines that explain an alert. See [notifications and emails](/war-room/alerts-and-emails/#bell).
